course: dictionary
lesson: 6765
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The context, the words around them, tells you which meaning the writer chose. Operation is a good example, because it has three different meanings.
explain: In maths, «all four operations» means add, subtract, multiply and divide. When you read a word problem, your first job is often to choose the right operation before you can solve it.
explain: In a hospital, an operation is a surgeon fixing something inside the body. In the news, a «rescue operation» is a planned piece of work done by many people. Look at the clues around the word to decide which meaning fits.
fact: Operation has three main meanings: a way of calculating in maths, a surgeon's work inside the body, and a planned piece of work done by many people.
fact: The four maths operations are add, subtract, multiply and divide.
fact: Some maths problems need two operations, so you may have to work out one step before you can take the next.
fact: A surgeon is the doctor who carries out an operation on the body.
fact: A «rescue operation» is a planned effort where many people work together to save people or animals.
exercise: «Sam had to choose the right operation to solve the problem.» In maths, what is an operation? | A place where people go to rest | A kind of soft, slow music | A bag used for shopping | *A way of working with numbers, such as add or divide
exercise: The surgeon got ready for the operation on the boy's arm. What does operation mean here? | *A surgeon fixing something inside the body | A loud noise from a machine | A type of warm blanket | A planned trip to the seaside
exercise: «The rescue operation saved everyone trapped in the cave.» What does operation mean here? | *A planned piece of work done by many people | A way to cook eggs | A type of sum with numbers | A sleepy feeling after lunch
test: «All four operations» in maths are add, subtract, multiply and divide. Which one is NOT an operation? | Subtract | *Hop | Divide | Add
test: «The team worked all night on the rescue operation.» Which word tells you the team was doing planned work to save people? | All | Night | *Rescue | Worked
exam: «The team worked all night on the rescue operation, with divers and helicopters.» Which clue shows that operation means planned work by many people? | Nothing, because operation only means maths | *Rescue, with divers and helicopters | The word night | The word all
